{
  "$comment": "#EXP-1639 (owner 2026-11-06, drafts approved; start = automatic for every running root session the member started): A RUNNING SESSION ON THE LOCK SCREEN ×2 (iOS ActivityKit Live Activity on the Lock Screen + Dynamic Island, a widget-extension target; Android an ongoing notification, on Android 16 a promoted `Notification.ProgressStyle` Live Update with a status-bar chip; web and desktop have none). Model = pure `liveActivityFollows` + `liveActivityContent` (src/live-activity.ts; iOS ExpPush `LiveActivityModel.swift`, linked by the widget extension, Android `data/push/LiveActivity.kt`), every mirror replays the `*Cases`. WHICH SESSIONS (`liveActivityFollows`): a ROOT session (no parent) the member STARTED by hand (its `userId`, no `startedByAgentId`), not an agent conversation (no `agentId`), whose phase is not `done`; at most `maxActivities` at once, the newest started first. PHASES: `needsInput` = `needsYou`, else `blocked` = `blocked`, else `queued` = `starting`, `running` = `working`, `idle` or `ended` = `done`. A follow STARTS when a session enters a non-done phase and ENDS at `done` (the last content stays `dismissMinutes`, then the OS removes it); the next turn starts a new one. THE CONTENT (`liveActivityContent`): `title` = the session's display title, or `copy.encryptedTitle` when the title is sealed (the phone fills the real one in locally from its own store when it can open it, never the server); `subtitle` = `copy.phases[phase]`, plus ` · ` + the device label when known; `detail` = for `needsYou` the question-push.json preview of a PLAINTEXT ask (null for a sealed one: the phone may fill it in locally), for `blocked` the blocked badge label, else null; `badge` = `needs-you` for `needsYou`, else `PR #<n>` when the session has an open PR, else `timer` (the OS counts up from `startedAt`); `segment` (Android ProgressStyle, `segments` in order) = 1 for starting/working/blocked, 2 needsYou, 3 when a PR is open and not done, 4 done. TRANSPORT, end to end like every push: the server SEALS the content (with `sessionId`, `phase`, `startedAt`) to the phone's push key (push-seal.json) and hands it to push-relay's `POST /activity` (`start` / `update` / `end`); iOS: the relay sends APNs `liveactivity` pushes whose content-state is ONLY that sealed blob (push-to-start with the install's start token, updates with the per-activity token the phone registered), and the widget extension opens it with the push key in the shared keychain, so neither the relay nor Apple ever read a title or a question; Android: a data-only FCM message the app opens and draws. The server sends only on a change of the content, at most once per `minUpdateSeconds` (a `needsYou` or `done` change goes out at once, high priority). Tapping it opens the session (inbox-route.json). OS-drawn: styleguide entry `os-live-activity`, not an Exponential UI primitive.",
